{
  "$comment": [
    "Frozen reference expectation table for the P4A parser spike (task 6.1).",
    "",
    "Derived from the verified Lezer reference dump (spike/parser-spike/explore/dump-lezer.mjs)",
    "cross-checked BY HAND against the known canonical fixture definitions in",
    "tests/byte-contract/generate-fixtures.mjs (the non-circular part of the round-trip gate).",
    "ALL candidates (TS + Rust) are validated against this same table.",
    "",
    "Semantics:",
    "- source: exact canonical source text the construct's sourceRange must slice to",
    "  (half-open [start,end) on the logical LF text, UTF-16 code units after conversion).",
    "- content: expected contentRange text. Exact string compare for inline kinds",
    "  (strong/emphasis/strikethrough/inlineCode/link/image/footnoteReference),",
    "  trim()-tolerant for block kinds (heading/listItem/taskCheckbox/fence/blockquote/",
    "  paragraph/table/frontmatter/htmlBlock/htmlComment). null = content not compared.",
    "- markers: exact delimiter strings the candidate's markerRanges must slice to,",
    "  as a multiset, when the candidate provides any. null = markers informational only.",
    "- alsoMatch: alternative kinds a candidate may use for the same construct",
    "  (e.g. footnoteReference vs link for '[^1]').",
    "- requireAll=false fixtures (malformed) record behavior only; every construct is",
    "  classified SPURIOUS/informational and no MISS is counted.",
    "",
    "Known intentional table facts (verified against parser output + fixture structure):",
    "- Lezer has no frontmatter node: syntax-frontmatter will show SPURIOUS setext-heading/",
    "  hr/link constructs; the frontmatter entry documents the REQUIRED correct construct.",
    "- '[^1]: footnote text' is a link reference definition under pure CommonMark and a",
    "  footnote definition when footnotes are enabled; both are acceptable via alsoMatch.",
    "- Link reference definitions produce NO events in pulldown-cmark (expected MISS)."
  ],
